 "remarks": "Historic character and modern conveniance converge at 96 Fitch Avenue, an exceptional residence in Darien's coveted Noroton neighborhood. Formerly home to the Wee Burn Country Club, this fully renovated property offers a rare combination of historic distinction, fully renovated turnkey property, and income-producing potential. The expansive first-floor residence features two bedrooms, two beautifully renovated baths, an updated kitchen, gracious living and dining rooms, and a walk-in closet. A wraparound covered porch and rear stone patio provide elegant settings for outdoor entertaining and quiet relaxation, while the attached one-car garage delivers effortless everyday convenience.  Two (or 3) legal rental apartments on each level create a unique stream of supplemental income and exceptional flexibility. Ideal for tenants, guests or extended family, these private spaces further enhance the property's versatility.  Embrace a walkable coastal lifestyle near Great Island, Weed and Pear Tree Point beaches, Hindley Elementary School, Noroton Heights train station, Roost, the Darien YMCA, and more. With its storied provenance, sophisticated renovations, and built-in income potential, 96 Fitch Avenue is a truly distinctive opportunity to own a piece of Darien history with the ease of modern living.",
